From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 03:13:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] let an async task inherit the context it was scheduled from

EssentialsXSpawn handles a join as PlayerJoinEvent (region thread) ->
runTaskAsynchronously -> delayedJoin -> scheduleSyncDelayedTask. On Paper the
last hop means "back to the main thread"; here the async pool thread has no
region context, so patch 0029 refuses it and everything after that line is
skipped - which on a first join is the newbie spawnpoint, the announcement and
the starter kit.

Measured on a username that had never joined: empty inventory, no announcement,
and the refusal fires on first joins only.

This is not an inference. 0029 asks "which thread is asking"; the only change is
that an async task now remembers the context it was created from, captured in
CraftAsyncTask's constructor - which still runs on the thread that asked, so the
context is a fact at that moment rather than something deduced later. Nothing
looks inside the Runnable, so DEC-19 B1 and N18 stay closed, and the thread's own
context always wins when it has one. Inheritance does not chain across a second
async hop.

The blast radius is exactly the tasks that are refused today: a task that never
schedules a sync task is untouched, and one that does is currently not running at
all. So this can only turn "never runs" into "runs on the region it came from",
with genuinely cross-region access still failing loudly at the access - the same
bargain DEC-54 accepted for 0029.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java
index e4e2e42d0ca25df7fe9f2dd4275610e45fcb2c84..5f53e298f79eae93a1ca92976f3a6e601d3cfc70 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftAsyncTask.java
@@ -11,6 +11,12 @@ class CraftAsyncTask extends CraftTask {
 
     private final LinkedList<BukkitWorker> workers = new LinkedList<BukkitWorker>();
     private final Map<Integer, CraftTask> runners;
+    // Lophinya start - carry the scheduling thread's context into this async task
+    // Captured here, not in run(): the constructor still runs on the thread that asked for the task,
+    // which is the only moment the context is a fact rather than a guess.
+    private final fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaCallerContextDispatch.CapturedContext lophinya$schedulingContext =
+        fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaCallerContextDispatch.captureCallerContext();
+    // Lophinya end
 
     CraftAsyncTask(final Map<Integer, CraftTask> runners, final Plugin plugin, final Object task, final int id, final long delay) {
         super(plugin, task, id, delay);
@@ -54,7 +60,9 @@ class CraftAsyncTask extends CraftTask {
         }
         Throwable thrown = null;
         try {
-            super.run();
+            // Lophinya start - make the scheduling thread's context visible for this body only
+            fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaCallerContextDispatch.runInherited(this.lophinya$schedulingContext, super::run);
+            // Lophinya end
         } catch (final Throwable t) {
             thrown = t;
             this.getOwner().getLogger().log(
